 ## Unreleased
 
+## 1.6.1
+
+### Upgrade notes
+
+- **Nothing to migrate or re-import.** The two schema changes are made at the
+  first start: the `th_upload` table that tracks an upload in flight (#279),
+  and a default for `tokens_valid_after` that applies to accounts created from
+  then on (#282); existing accounts and their sessions are untouched. Every
+  other change is in how stored readings are read and named, so a series
+  printed in two units, a device metric's name and the journal's names are
+  right as soon as the new image runs. Upgrade a Docker install with `git pull` and `./deploy.sh`, with the
+  same `COMPOSE_PROFILES` it was started with (`COMPOSE_PROFILES=local-cpu
+  ./deploy.sh` for the local stack); it pulls
+  `thetahealth4mirobody/mirobody:1.6.1`.
+- **A file 1.6.0 listed 已处理 with no readings stays that way** (#275): the
+  upgrade does not read it again. Once the setup page shows the model ready,
+  choose 重新处理 on its row in 数据 › 文件 (`POST /api/v1/data/reprocess-file`),
+  which reads it again from the stored file. Uploading it again works too: the
+  text cache keeps only text that was read, and no reading was written. A
+  report 1.6.0 read with a scanner's settings among its readings (#235) keeps
+  them until it is read again the same way.
+
 ### Changed
 
 - **MCP directories have less to get wrong.** Directories that mirror the MCP
@@ -59,6 +81,24 @@
 
 ### Fixed
 
+- **The journal names a coded reading as the indicator list does.** On a
+  Chinese page, a sentence logged in 数据 › 记录 such as
+  "昨晚开始头疼，血压150/95" came back as `收缩压 150 mmHg → Systolic blood pressure
+  8480-6`: `GET /api/v1/journal` and `POST /api/v1/journal/sentence` sent only
+  `display`, LOINC's long name, so the journal stayed English after 1.6.0 named
+  the same code 收缩压 in the indicator list (#231). Now a LOINC-coded entry in
+  both answers carries `label` from `standardize.label_for` in the request's
+  language, the one name `GET /api/v1/health-indicators` gives the same code, and the web client shows it with
+  `display` as its tooltip, falling back to `display`; a language switch
+  reloads the feed. An English page reads as before: LOINC gives vital signs
+  no English consumer name, so they keep `Systolic blood pressure`, and a code
+  with one (`Heart rate`) shows it. An ICPC-3 complaint gets no `label` in any
+  language and keeps WONCA's English term (头疼 → `Headache NS01`): the bundle
+  holds no Chinese ICPC-3 title, and ICPC-3 is CC BY-ND, so writing our own
+  would be a derivative we may not publish (`res/icpc3/icpc3.NOTICE`). The web
+  side is thetahealth/mirobody-web #27, already in `frontend/`. To tell: with
+  `X-Language: zh-CN`, a journal entry coded 8480-6 answers
+  `"label": "收缩压"`; with `X-Language: en` it has no `label`.
 - **A scanner's settings and a record's history headings are no longer
   readings** (part of #235). Chinese check-up PDFs left `AO%`, `D`, `DR`,
   `FR`, `Frd`, `Frq`, `Gn`, `PAT TIS` and `S/A` in the indicator list. These
@@ -180,6 +220,23 @@
   catalogue and the raw readings already did, and stats rows sort by it. How
   to tell: `view=stats` over two device metrics lists both by name, the same
   names the catalogue shows.
+- **A reinstalled stack neither locks out its first account nor lets an old
+  token into it.** A stack started again on a new database (`docker compose
+  down -v`, then `./deploy.sh`) keeps `.env`, and so its signing key, and
+  numbers accounts from 1 again. A browser still holding a token from before
+  had two outcomes. If it asked before anyone signed up, the server found no
+  such account and remembered the id as closed for as long as it ran; the
+  next person to sign up got that id, and every token they were given was
+  refused: sign-up answered ok and the page went back to the sign-in form,
+  with a 401 in the console. If it asked after, the old token opened the new
+  account. Found while testing 1.6.1 on a reinstalled local stack. Now a new
+  account refuses every token minted before it existed (`tokens_valid_after`
+  defaults to its creation, less the minute `iat` allows for clock skew), and
+  an id with no account is looked up again on the next request; an account
+  closed in Settings is still refused for good. Accounts that already exist
+  are unchanged. How to tell: with the old page open, run `docker compose
+  down -v` and `./deploy.sh`, then sign up; the data page opens, and the old
+  page's token is refused.
 
